)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(t - 3)j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t + 1)k \\\\ &= (2 t)\\,i+(1)\\,j+(2)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(2 t)^2+(1)^2+(2)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y + 2 z^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=-2\\left((t^{2})(t - 3)-(2 t + 1)^2\\right) \\\\ &= -2\\left(1t^3+(-3)t^2-\\left(4t^2+(4)t+1\\right)\\right) \\\\ &= - 2 t^{3} + 14 t^{2} + 8 t + 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}(- 2 t^{3} + 14 t^{2} + 8 t + 2)(\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{1}^{\\frac{3}{2}}2 \\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- t^{3} + 7 t^{2} + 4 t + 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539129 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539150 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539129 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539129 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to $\\int_C x y - z^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2}, 2 t + 2, 3 t + 1\\rangle$ for $0\\le t\\le 2$?" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539129 1072 #uuid "1b6b1bd1-88e4-5d2e-9dfb-33372f16d858" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539129 1074 "Since $r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2}, 2 t + 2, 3 t + 1\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=2 t^{2}$, $y=2 t + 2$, $z=3 t + 1$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,k \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t^{2})i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t + 2)j+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(3 t + 1)k \\\\ &= (4 t)\\,i+(2)\\,j+(3)\\,k \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}z}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(4 t)^2+(2)^2+(3)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=x y - z^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=(2 t^{2})(2 t + 2)-(3 t + 1)^2 \\\\ &= 4t^3+(4)t^2-\\left(9t^2+(6)t+1\\right) \\\\ &= 4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y,z)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{0}^{2} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{0}^{2}(4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1)(\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{0}^{2}\\sqrt{16 t^{2} + 13} \\left(4 t^{3} - 5 t^{2} - 6 t - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539130 1080 "\\int_{2}^{\\frac{11}{2}}\\frac{2 t^{2}}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539130 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539130 1083 #uuid "1bbf7d63-fae5-55c0-b85a-adf23a9e249f" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539131 1080 "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}10 t \\cos{\\left(2 t \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539131 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539131 1083 #uuid "1ddac435-f4c5-5790-a848-0d7fd8aecc12" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186539130 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186539144 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186539181 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186539187 13