80 "\\int_{0}^{5}\\frac{2 t}{\\sqrt{4 t^{2} + 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539199 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539199 1083 #uuid "e8983d55-5bea-5b37-b969-63bf075c738a" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539200 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539125 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539200 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539200 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s,$ where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j\\,$ for $1\\le t\\le \\frac{4}{3}?$" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539200 1072 #uuid "f04c0a98-4a6c-5873-883f-948e18d8b72b" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539200 1074 "Since $r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j,$ then along the curve we have $x=t$ and $y={t}^{2}.$ \n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+2tj \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, if  $f(x,y)=\\frac{x}{4y+1}$, then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\frac{x}{4y+1}\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}(\\frac{t}{4{t}^{2}+1})\\cdot \\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\frac{4}{3}}\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+1}}\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539201 1080 "$\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(8 t^{3} + t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t$." 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539201 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539201 1083 #uuid "f38f729c-48d5-5112-b120-4a7a2e085fed" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539202 1068 #edb/ref 17592186539183 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539202 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539202 1071 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_C2\\left((x^{3} - y)\\right)ds$, where the curve $C$ is parametrized by $r(t) = 2ti + (2 - t)j$ for $- \\frac{3}{2}\\le t\\le 2$?" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539202 1072 #uuid "f515b153-b2d5-5f07-b698-2b223e35049e" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539202 1074 "Since $r(t)=\\langle 2 t, 2 - t\\rangle,$ then along the curve we have $x=2 t$, $y=2 - t$.\n\nComputing $r'(t)$ and $\\|r'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r'(t)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t}\\,j \\\\ &= \\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 t)i+\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}t}(2 - t)j \\\\ &= (2)\\,i+(-1)\\,j \\\\ \\|r'(t)\\|&=\\sqrt{(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2+(\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}t})^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{(2)^2+(-1)^2} \\\\ &= \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2 x^{3} - 2 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t))&=2\\left((2 t)^3-(2 - t)\\right) \\\\ &= 2\\left(8t^3-2+t\\right) \\\\ &= 16 t^{3} + 2 t - 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}s&=\\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2} f(r(t))\\,\\|r'(t)\\|\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}(16 t^{3} + 2 t - 4)(\\sqrt{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int_{- \\frac{3}{2}}^{2}2 \\sqrt{5} \\left(8 t^{3} + t - 2\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535899 17592186045443 true] [17592186539203 1080 "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{5}{2}}2 \\sqrt{36 t^{2} + 5} \\left(- 3 t^{2} \\